  "result": "The session length is set in one place. The \"it has expired\" check actually happens in two places, one after the other.\n\n**At sign-in:** `createSessionToken` in `src/server/services/session-service.ts` sets the expiry to now plus `SESSION_TTL_DAYS`, which is 30 days (defined on line 17). A user who signed in a month ago is right at that limit.\n\n**On a later request:**\n- `src/server/repositories/session-repository.ts:64` returns `null` when the session's `expiresAt` is now or earlier. This check runs first.\n- `src/lib/session.ts:30` checks again in `getSessionPrincipal` and returns `null` unless `expiresAt` is still in the future.\n\nEither one returning `null` means there is no signed-in user, so they're sent to sign-in. I've listed both files because they both enforce the cutoff. If you only count the first check, drop `src/lib/session.ts`.\n\nANSWER: src/server/services/session-service.ts, src/server/repositories/session-repository.ts, src/lib/session.ts",
